# Cursor AI Rules - AI Agent Study Guide

> Documentation repository studying OpenAI Codex-RS TUI architecture for building AI coding agents.

---

## Project Overview

This is a **documentation-only** repository. No implementation code should be created.

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Purpose | Study OpenAI Codex-RS TUI architecture |
| Type | Documentation repository |
| Source | https://github.com/openai/codex |
| Primary Output | Mermaid diagrams, markdown documentation |

### Goals

1. Document the communication flow between Codex-RS components
2. Extract reusable patterns for AI coding agents
3. Provide clear architecture diagrams with source references
4. Create templates for LLM-optimizing other projects

---

## Entry Points

Read files in this priority order:

| Priority | File | Purpose |
|----------|------|---------|
| 1 | `AGENTS.md` | AI agent instructions and coordination |
| 2 | `llms.txt` | Documentation index for LLM consumption |
| 3 | `llms-full.txt` | Complete context dump |
| 4 | `docs/WORKFLOWS.md` | Task execution steps |
| 5 | `docs/architecture-diagram.md` | Primary technical reference |

### Subdirectory Context

When working in `docs/`, also read `docs/AGENTS.md` for local context.

