## Naming Conventions

### Documentation Files

| Pattern | Example | Usage |
|---------|---------|-------|
| SCREAMING_SNAKE.md | `CONCEPTS.md` | Core documentation |
| kebab-case.md | `architecture-diagram.md` | Technical diagrams |
| AGENTS.md | `docs/AGENTS.md` | Subdirectory context |

### Content Naming

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---------|------------|---------|
| Sections | Title Case | `## Key Insights` |
| Code references | backticks | `codex-rs/tui/src/app.rs` |
| Component names | PascalCase | `ThreadManager`, `CodexThread` |
| Enum variants | PascalCase | `UserTurn`, `TurnComplete` |

---

## Documentation Patterns

### Tables for Mappings

Always use tables for:
- File locations
- Component responsibilities
- Type definitions
- Command references

```markdown
| Component | Location | Purpose |
|-----------|----------|---------|
| App | `codex-rs/tui/src/app.rs` | Main TUI struct |
```

### Code Blocks with Context

Include file paths in code blocks:

```markdown
```rust
// codex-rs/protocol/src/protocol.rs
pub enum Op {
    UserTurn { items: Vec<UserInput> },
    // ...
}
```
```

### Mermaid Diagrams

Include participant labels with file paths:

```markdown
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant App as App<br/>(tui/app.rs)
    participant TM as ThreadManager<br/>(core/thread_manager.rs)
```
```

### Source Links

Always include GitHub source links:

```markdown
**Source**: [codex-rs/tui/src/app.rs](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/tui/src/app.rs)
```

---

## Common Tasks

### Task 1: Add New Diagram

1. Open `docs/architecture-diagram.md`
2. Add new section with Mermaid diagram
3. Include participant labels with file paths
4. Validate: `./scripts/render-diagrams.sh`
5. Update `llms.txt` with new content reference

### Task 2: Update Documentation

1. Read current content
2. Check cross-references in `llms.txt`
3. Make changes maintaining style consistency
4. Update `llms.txt` and `llms-full.txt`
5. Verify with `glow docs/[file].md`

### Task 3: Add New Concept

1. Determine target file:
   - Pattern → `docs/PATTERNS.md`
   - Term → `docs/GLOSSARY.md`
   - Concept → `docs/CONCEPTS.md`
2. Follow existing format in target file
3. Include source file reference
4. Update indexes

### Task 4: Verify Repository

```bash
./scripts/render-diagrams.sh        # Validate Mermaid
glow docs/architecture-diagram.md   # Preview content
open docs/codex-architecture.html   # View rendered diagrams
```

