## Critical Architecture Facts

### TUI Communication Path

```
CORRECT:  TUI App → ThreadManager → CodexThread → Codex
WRONG:    TUI App → MessageProcessor → ThreadManager
```

**MessageProcessor is ONLY for external JSON-RPC clients (VS Code extension).**

### Key Types

| Type | Direction | Purpose |
|------|-----------|---------|
| `Op` enum | Input to agent | User operations (UserTurn, ExecApproval, Interrupt) |
| `EventMsg` enum | Output from agent | Agent events (TurnStarted, TurnComplete, AgentMessage) |
| `Event` struct | Wrapper | Contains id + EventMsg |

### Component Layers

```
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│  TUI Layer (presentation)   │  codex-rs/tui/
├─────────────────────────────┤
│  Core Layer (business)      │  codex-rs/core/
├─────────────────────────────┤
│  Protocol Layer (contract)  │  codex-rs/protocol/
├─────────────────────────────┤
│  App Server (external)      │  codex-rs/app-server/
└─────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### Documentation Anti-Patterns

| Anti-Pattern | Correct Approach |
|--------------|------------------|
| Verbose explanations | Concise, use tables |
| Missing source links | Always include GitHub links |
| Outdated Codex-RS info | Verify against current source |
| Unvalidated Mermaid | Run render-diagrams.sh |
| Orphaned content | Update llms.txt after changes |

### Code Example Anti-Patterns

| Anti-Pattern | Correct Approach |
|--------------|------------------|
| Implementation code | Only documentation and examples |
| Code without file path | Include source file in comment |
| Untested examples | Verify against actual Codex-RS source |

---

## Quality Checklist

Before completing any documentation task:

- [ ] Mermaid diagrams render without errors
- [ ] Source file paths included in code blocks
- [ ] GitHub links are valid
- [ ] llms.txt updated
- [ ] llms-full.txt updated (if significant changes)
- [ ] Consistent with existing documentation style
- [ ] Tables used for mappings
- [ ] No implementation code created

---

## Key Codex-RS Components

### TUI Layer (`codex-rs/tui/`)

| Component | File | Purpose |
|-----------|------|---------|
| App | `app.rs` | Main application struct, event loop |
| ChatWidget | `chatwidget.rs` | Message display |
| ChatComposer | `bottom_pane/chat_composer.rs` | Input handling |
| ApprovalOverlay | `bottom_pane/approval_overlay.rs` | Approval UI |
| AppEvent | `app_event.rs` | Internal event types |

### Core Layer (`codex-rs/core/`)

| Component | File | Purpose |
|-----------|------|---------|
| ThreadManager | `thread_manager.rs` | Thread lifecycle |
| CodexThread | `codex_thread.rs` | Agent wrapper |
| Codex | `codex.rs` | Agent implementation |
| Session | `session.rs` | Session state |

### Protocol Layer (`codex-rs/protocol/`)

| Type | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| Op | Operations submitted to agent |
| EventMsg | Events emitted by agent |
| Event | Wrapper with id + msg |

### App Server (`codex-rs/app-server/`)

| Component | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| MessageProcessor | JSON-RPC handling |
| CodexMessageProcessor | Codex-specific handlers |

